silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_mittens_instance a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.flat.sections.02_mittens_anchor.concrete_anchor.mittens_instance" .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_mittens_instance silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensGovernedCatIndividual is Mittens is the governed individual cat — the colimit apex of D_Mittens. In the taxonomy diagram, this is the leftmost instancenode. Mittens is NOT the taxon row, NOT the storage key, NOT the catalog trace. It is the individual cat whose vet records, storage packets, and graph assertions are the cocone legs." .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_domesticcat_type_seed a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.flat.sections.02_mittens_anchor.concrete_anchor.domesticcat_type_seed" .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_domesticcat_type_seed silm:hasLongDescription "The DomesticCatClassificationSeed is DomesticCat type seed is the schemanode — the local classification bridge from Mittens toward the taxonomy. It is NOT Mittens and NOT the taxon row. It is the intermediate step: Mittens is classified through DomesticCat before reaching the full Felis catus taxonomy." .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_taxonomy_witness a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.flat.sections.02_mittens_anchor.concrete_anchor.taxonomy_witness" .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_taxonomy_witness silm:hasLongDescription "The FelisFelidaeWitnessSource is The taxonomy witness is the infonode — the source authority for the Felis catus classification. It must be preserved as a source witness before use; the complete name, parent path (Felis -> Felidae -> Carnivora -> Mammalia), and TSN must travel together." .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_felis_catus_tsn a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.flat.sections.02_mittens_anchor.concrete_anchor.felis_catus_tsn" .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_felis_catus_tsn silm:hasLongDescription "The FelisCatusTaxonWithTSN is Felis catus / TSN 183798 is the classnode — the complete taxonomic identifier for domestic cat. It is a SOURCE LEG into D_Mittens, not the identity of Mittens. A bare 'catus' match without the full taxon path is a regression test failure." .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_d_mittens_source_leg a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.flat.sections.02_mittens_anchor.concrete_anchor.d_mittens_source_leg" .
silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_flat_sections_02_mittens_anchor_concrete_anchor_d_mittens_source_leg silm:hasLongDescription "The D_MittensIndexedSourceLeg is D_Mittens source leg is the terminalnode in the taxonomy diagram — where the taxon row enters the source diagram as one indexed leg. The taxonomy leg contributes to D_Mittens but does not replace the colimit apex Mittens." .
